From: supavise <supavise@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] fix(studio): the Edge Function tester accepts the
 project hosts of a deployment without TLS

NIMBUS_PROD_PROJECTS_URL names the hosts of project APIs for the tester,
but the check built an https-only expression from it and allowed letters
only, so a deployment with no TLS (http project URLs) or a project host
with a digit or hyphen got Provided URL is not a valid Supabase edge
function URL for its own functions. The scheme now follows the value,
and the label may hold digits and hyphens. The host still has to be one
label under the configured apex.
---
 apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.test.ts | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.ts      | 20 ++++++++--
 2 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.test.ts b/apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.test.ts
index 0d6a43d8..7827e326 100644
--- a/apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.test.ts
+++ b/apps/studio/lib/api/edgeFunctions.test.ts
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@ import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest'
 import {
   buildDatabaseEdgeFunctionUrl,
